cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the n = 6 affine equivalence class data or tables from this site, please cite the PhD thesis below."
title: "Boolean Functions for Cryptography: affine equivalence class data (booleanfunction.github.io)"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Fuller
    given-names: Joanne
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5221-3505"
url: "https://booleanfunction.github.io"
repository-code: "https://github.com/booleanfunction/booleanfunction.github.io"
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-14"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Representative truth tables for all 150,357 affine equivalence classes of Boolean
  functions on six variables, grouped by nonlinearity, algebraic order and maximum
  absolute autocorrelation, together with the 74,542 classes that contain balanced
  functions. The data was computed for the PhD thesis "Analysis of Affine Equivalent
  Boolean Functions for Cryptography" (J. Fuller, Queensland University of Technology,
  2003) and first published on the Boolean Planet website in 2003; it is re-released here
  unchanged after re-validation. This archive also contains the booleanfunction.github.io
  website: class tables for n = 3, 4, 5, class sizes (self-mapping constant), the Theorem
  of Connectivity, constructions and search, linear redundancy in the AES S-box, and
  interactive tools (class graph explorer and function analyser).
keywords:
  - Boolean functions
  - cryptography
  - affine equivalence
  - nonlinearity
  - equivalence classes
